From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starling dev <starling@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: never capture transient uid-0 cgraphs

Only persistent ReplayGraph instances receive stable nonzero uids and may
use ggml-CUDA graph capture. Transient uid==0 cgraphs are one-shot graphs
whose nodes[0] pointer key collides across unrelated graphs when the
engine rebuilds per call; capturing them replays stale buffer addresses
(non-deterministic garbage). Such graphs now execute directly.
---
 src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -4745,10 +4745,17 @@
 #ifdef USE_CUDA_GRAPH
     graph_key = ggml_cuda_graph_get_key(cgraph);
 
-    ggml_cuda_graph_set_enabled(cuda_ctx, graph_key);
+    // Starling: only persistent graphs (stable nonzero uid) may capture.
+    // Transient uid==0 cgraphs are one-shot graphs whose nodes[0] pointer key
+    // collides across unrelated graphs when the engine rebuilds per call;
+    // capturing them replays stale buffer addresses (non-deterministic
+    // garbage). See patch 0008 in Starling's ggml-patches series.
+    if (cgraph->uid != 0) {
+        ggml_cuda_graph_set_enabled(cuda_ctx, graph_key);
+    }
 
     ggml_cuda_graph * graph = cuda_ctx->cuda_graph(graph_key);
-    if (graph->is_enabled()) {
+    if (cgraph->uid != 0 && graph->is_enabled()) {
         // Steady-state replay fast-path. When a graph has already completed
         // warmup AND carries a stable nonzero uid that matches the uid we saw
         // on the previous call, the graph is provably unchanged: its topology
